The same eleven types as the firing archive, declared the same way, each reaching
a function or a method of a package the class does not name instead of its
destination. Nothing in this archive flows into reflection, an encoder, a template
engine, a scan, the sort interface or a logging call, and the one type converted to
the log-value interface reaches the class by that conversion no more than the
others, so the class records nothing.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/flow

go 1.27.1
-- json.go --
package flow

import "sync"

// JSONPayload reaches no encoder.
type JSONPayload struct {
	Name   string `json:"name"`
	Extra  int
	secret string `json:"secret"`
}

// Describe is exported.
func (p JSONPayload) Describe() string { return p.Name }

func (p JSONPayload) hidden() int { return p.Extra }

// StoreJSON hands a value to an unrelated package.
func StoreJSON(m *sync.Map, p JSONPayload) { m.Store("json", p) }
